&lt;h2&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver the power, cooling and capacity that enable Graphcore’s engineers to bring up and test AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Bristol, you’ll lead regional lab and data centre infrastructure delivery and own operational readiness. As Graphcore’s client-side representative, you’ll turn agreed engineering requirements into practical delivery plans and improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will keep existing environments effective while creating capacity for testing and experimentation. You’ll identify constraints before they affect engineering work and improve reliability for high-density AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll guide builds, expansions and upgrades from site assessment through design, installation, commissioning and handover. You’ll manage approved budgets, supplier commitments, schedules and delivery risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an individual contributor, you’ll use independent technical judgement to balance regional projects with day-to-day operations. Experience with liquid cooling and pressurised infrastructure is particularly relevant to this work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll agree regional priorities with Systems Engineering, hardware engineering, IT, facilities, health and safety, and finance. You’ll coordinate internal teams and suppliers, making readiness, capacity constraints, costs and risks clear.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll resolve competing priorities and escalate changes that need additional investment or wider decisions. Working with counterparts in other regions, you’ll share improvements and apply consistent infrastructure standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading client-side infrastructure projects in data centres, labs or mission-critical environments, including hyperscale or high-performance computing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data centre power distribution, cooling, rack infrastructure, connectivity and building requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding projects through design, procurement, construction, commissioning and operational handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret engineering drawings and technical specifications, and assess supplier proposals against agreed requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management skills covering budgets, schedules, dependencies and risks, alongside infrastructure capacity planning and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication across technical and non-technical teams, with experience coordinating suppliers and resolving competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible working:&lt;/strong&gt; Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
